  "title": "Chapter 9 – Hand Tools and Their Uses",
  "order": 8,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "jr3fh0s",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Hand tools are classified by function into striking, holding, driving, cutting, and measuring tools.",
        "Hammers are designated by their weight and peen shape (ball-peen, cross-peen, straight-peen).",
        "Spanners and pliers provide mechanical advantage for gripping, turning, and cutting fasteners or wires.",
        "Files remove thin layers of metal and are specified by length, grade, cut, and shape.",
        "Hacksaws and cold chisels serve as primary manual cutting tools for metals and structural shapes."
      ],
      "id": "6tj9j4u"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Tool Categories",
          "value": "5 Main Types",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Common Striking Tool",
          "value": "Ball-Peen Hammer",
          "icon": "award"
        },
        {
          "label": "Key Cutting Tools",
          "value": "Files & Chisels",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
          "label": "Core Priority",
          "value": "Safety & Care",
          "icon": "info"
        }
      ],
      "id": "ceat32b"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gvtkffr",
      "content": "Hand tools are manually operated tools used in workshops for operations such as cutting, shaping, tightening, gripping, measuring, and assembling materials. They do not require electricity or external power and are widely used in trades like fitter, electrician, mechanic, carpenter, welder, and plumber."
    },
